                <pb facs="0782" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6739: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-12T16:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 13—9:52
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Serious fighting took place yesterday at Hailar between Chinese and Japanese
                    troops as a result of the arrest by Japanese of certain Russian railway workmen
                    whom Chinese demanded be released. Chinese greatly outnumbered Japanese and are
                    now in control Hailar Station. Japanese have greatly increased number troops at
                    three stations between Harbin and Changchun. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
